<task>
You are analyzing a screenshot of a web page that is blocking an automated job application. The page requires human intervention. Your job is to identify the form fields the user needs to fill out and return a structured layout describing those fields.
</task>

<context>
User action type: {{.UserAction}}
Action details: {{.ActionDetails}}
</context>

<instructions>
Analyze the screenshot and identify all form fields the user needs to interact with to resolve the blocking page.

For each field, provide:
- field_name: A human-readable label for the field (e.g. "Username", "Password", "OTP Code", "CAPTCHA Text")
- type: The HTML input type if applicable (e.g. "text", "password", "number", "email", "tel"). Null if not an input.
- component: The UI component type (e.g. "input", "textarea", "select", "radio", "checkbox"). Null if unknown.
- options: For select/radio/checkbox fields, provide the available options as an array. Null otherwise.

Common patterns by action type:
- USER_ACTION_CAPTCHA: Usually a single text input for the CAPTCHA solution
- USER_ACTION_AUTHENTICATION: Usually username/email + password fields, sometimes "remember me" checkbox
- USER_ACTION_OTP: Usually a single numeric input for the OTP code
</instructions>

<response_format>
Respond with a JSON array of field objects. Example:
[
  {"field_name": "Email", "type": "email", "component": "input", "options": null},
  {"field_name": "Password", "type": "password", "component": "input", "options": null}
]

If the page has no identifiable form fields (e.g. a pure CAPTCHA image with no input), return a single field:
[{"field_name": "CAPTCHA Solution", "type": "text", "component": "input", "options": null}]
</response_format>